Core task complete — Mandelbrot deep-zoom viewer with perturbation theory.

Built & validated this spawn:
- Mobile-first JS+HTML+CSS viewer (index.html, styles.css, src/*).
- Perturbation theory: BigInt high-precision reference orbit + double-precision
  delta iteration + Zhuoran rebasing (glitch-free), reference auto-selection,
  Pauldelbrot glitch detection.
- VALIDATED vs a BigInt-exact ground-truth oracle to +/-1 iteration at
  2^45, 2^120, 2^400, plus full-pipeline deep renders.
- Engine dispatch: naive doubles (shallow) / perturbation (deep). See NOTES for
  the empirical reason (shallow perturbation has no precision advantage).
- Multi-worker render pool (reference once + parallel row-bands), progressive
  coarse->fine. ~8x faster deep render.
- UI: pinch/pan/double-tap, 4 palettes, iteration slider, URL-hash bookmarks,
  coordinate Go box.
- Tests: 26 Node unit (npm test) + 18 Playwright e2e mobile+desktop (npm run e2e),
  all green. Screenshots in screenshots/ confirm correct renders.

